for them.

Marc Skinner=E2=80=99s exit after a frustrating five years in Manchester wa=
s welcomed by sections of their fanbase but the manager arguably helped the=
 side to punch well above their weight, with a comparatively small wage bil=
l despite a competitive turnover. Eva Olid is an exciting young manager, ha=
ving led Hearts from the bottom of the Scottish Women=E2=80=99s Premier Lea=
gue (with the team avoiding relegation only because of league expansion) to=
 the title before her departure at the end of last season. However, if fans=
 are hoping for a fresh start they should perhaps temper their excitement, =
with the club leaning into Olid=E2=80=99s reputation for player development=
 and their four summer recruits so far not doing anywhere near enough to of=
fset the loss of their outgoing players.


Eva Olid talks to the media on the eve of the new WSL season. Photograph: P=
oppy Townson/MUFC/Manchester United/Getty Images


They could be troubled by a chasing pack who have invested shrewdly, in the=
 case of Tottenham, Everton, Liverpool and Brighton, or boldly, in the case=
 of London City Lionesses.

