ograph: Tony Smith/Alamy


Aston Villa have recruited 10 to replace the nine departed players but the =
fear will be that the incoming players struggle to fill the hole left by pl=
ayers such as Hanson, Ebony Salmon and Gabi Nunes.

Of the newcomers to the WSL, Birmingham and Crystal Palace have overseen si=
milarly large squad turnovers, with some top-level talent brought in to att=
empt to ensure they avoid the drop back down to WSL 2 such as Millie Turner=
 and Lisa Naalsund for the former and Bethany England for the latter.

Charlton have not been able to recruit so ambitiously in the summer, though=
 eight new players have arrived to help the manager, Karen Hills, and her s=
ide who hope to leave egg on the faces of many who have put them as favouri=
tes to go down.

Predicting results or the outcome of the season is nigh- on impossible thou=
gh, and that will be the hope: that the expanded league delivers surprises.

