<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Three league games played, <a href=3D"http=
s://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7=
fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgYah5jsyKKBNhx6-BYFiHJAC5PU03gRXQyg-grgl=
Rit_RZgve-vHxneK8zvZ8OzYIB_8N4trlct0vD1FOS9xwyNIaxq_UJL5pV2DJWJzOeEGs-RVZZj=
3NnlqnDUfvLOEVouEg6b_kDTlkgxu0me1dqMwlwbnSZnXffCMSkN2ZxWvSwdKVlll9EWv-Of7CR=
-f3i1MonC8iSMHZ1nQ_zuCMTaKpKeEhS1bU2bzSSBvtaUwMHVCFfEHtTHoB7jtL3iit/4tu/wD6=
GdGHqSX2-_xsDsJ7QRw/h14/h001.UjMAUugi8DL_TZjJEY9WrGBeqkLqZYrHcn3a_Z76N3o" s=
tyle=3D"color: #0077B6;">three games won</a>. For Arsenal this season could=
 only have started better if Manchester City, who look like being one of th=
eir two most serious challengers, had dropped points. But it=E2=80=99s not =
just about results: Arsenal have been comfortably the better side in each o=
f those three games, approaching each of them in very different ways.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">After the controlled victory over Coventry=
 City and the tight game against Aston Villa that was won thanks to ratchet=
ing up the pressure in the 15 minutes after half-time, came success in a fa=
r more open game in which they conceded for the first time this season. Che=
lsea tested Arsenal on Sunday, went ahead, and yet Mikel Arteta=E2=80=99s s=
ide still always looked like they would win =E2=80=93 even if it did take a=
 superb late save from David Raya to keep out an Estev=C3=A3o shot. But the=
 goalkeeper too is part of their strength; even if an opposing team can wor=
k a shooting opportunity, Raya has the capacity for spectacular saves that =
can dispirit opponents.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Arsenal threatened from set-pieces but als=
o from open play; they can beat opponents in multiple different ways, even =
when Declan Rice, probably their player of the season last year, has an off=
 day (his unpunished late trip on Morgan Rogers was cynical and nasty, one =
of those deliberate offences miles from the ball that the game would benefi=
t from treating as a red card offence).</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The uplift may simply be confidence, <a hr=
ef=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG1=
8IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgr4JEaGEkiPlxdISPxzlC81gx-w2Xo=
uluxLPxr7YGtnQAK4F3V7lcGnalLDkwDzqda3Pk1yx604ebwTpkc9sxaHcbL3LVvUlTv99mV-KR=
cfbz6Z-W4leedjH02eSXpNZRqdLO5VkZCBL3-roEOQq-jGoUMIwqWcI0Xyf8EN-JDexxfc9RNBM=
bSB-GpOJw_mMsvi_BPXQT8X34e916oSW9XsxjeMrk-OxzghZ-_36PbqFTRLf_7dvwhaFjaPVn4X=
OOgX4HhqGkmro6-CxYMc2c1g/4tu/wD6GdGHqSX2-_xsDsJ7QRw/h15/h001.N5MHiK-unBaaAJ=
CWKDPIS7NFsOqaDkAozlOfaLpoqJc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the pressure of no=
t having won the title</a>, of those three successive second-place finishes=
, now lifted. But there are also individuals who look sharper, livelier, fr=
esher than they did at any point last season. Martin =C3=98degaard is perha=
ps the most obvious. He struggled with injuries last season and scored only=
 one goal; already this season he has two in the league and one in the Comm=
unity Shield. Some players return from the World Cup and look exhausted or =
find the readaptation to the grind of the domestic game difficult; =C3=98de=
gaard seems reinvigorated.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There is an imagination to his play, a lig=
htness, and he took his goal against Chelsea superbly. His link-ups with Ka=
i Havertz, another at times mercurial presence, were often delightful, conj=
uring space and angles where none seemed to exist and bringing the winner. =
In a team that last season developed a reputation for uncompromising physic=
ality, there is something almost otherworldly about seeing two such ephemer=
al talents combining, sprites glimmering on a castle wall.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But it=E2=80=99s not just =C3=98degaard. F=
or Bukayo Saka, last season felt like chickens coming home to roost. He is =
only 25 but Sunday brought what was already his 205th league start, while p=
laying regularly for England as well. Fatigue had been stored up, which is =
always a worry for players who emerge as early as he did. Thomas Tuchel did=
n=E2=80=99t use him in the World Cup semi-final for reasons of tiredness or=
 injury that remain opaque (the situation was promptly confused when he sco=
red a hat-trick in the third-place game). But he seems back to something li=
ke his best in the early weeks of this season, fizzing in from the right-ha=
nd side and delivering dangerous corners on demand.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The other standout in the early weeks of t=
he season is Riccardo Calafiori, who has already developed a very promising=
 relationship going forward with Christos Tzolis, even if a few issues rema=
in to be resolved defensively on that flank. The Italian, who scored Arsena=
l=E2=80=99s opener in the Community Shield, is not only a threat from set-p=
lays but is very good at breaking through the lines, making him a real weap=
on against low blocks.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Chelsea are improving. Xabi Alonso=E2=80=
=99s side were far less open through midfield than they had been against Fu=
lham and Brighton =E2=80=93 easier as that can sometimes be to manage again=
st sides who don=E2=80=99t instinctively cede possession. It may be, especi=
ally as the attrition of European fixtures strikes others later in the seas=
on, that they emerge as a very serious force. Arsenal, though, are very, ve=
ry good now, and that means they could be several points clear by the time =
that putative Chelsea challenge emerges.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Arteta=E2=80=99s side are not merely playi=
ng with great authority; the fixtures have also fallen well for them, getti=
ng Villa away and Chelsea at home while both sides are still finding their =
patterns of play. It=E2=80=99s still very early. We haven=E2=80=99t even go=
t to the first international break yet. Pitfalls are always waiting, and fo=
otball is not a sport that reacts well to being taken for granted. But for =
Arsenal, their title defence could hardly have started better. Things could=
 change but, at this moment, it seems more likely that they=E2=80=99ll have=
